# Device patch series. Application order matters: the boot ladder has to be
# the very last patch applied, because its insertion points sit in the context
# that native-4k-bootstrap-capacity.patch and zzz-boot-progress.patch use for
# their own reverse checks. Paths are relative to this file.
#
# 0008..0015 replace the twelve iOS-17-only ARM64 patches that do not apply to
# XNU 8796 (guard both the Apple tunables include and its APPLY_TUNABLES call,
# gate the Apple AMCC objects,
# widen pmap_sync_page_attributes_phys' physical shift, drop an Apple-clang
# flag the Linux clang rejects, take the pointee type without dereferencing a
# C++ void pointer, carry the DriverKit generator's IORPC.kernelContent, and
# replace the over-aligned uio_stackbuf_t array with a rounded uint64_t one)
# and come before the board fix, which needs native-smp-secondary's MAX_CPUS.
# 0016 restores the -MJ compile records in makedefs/MakeInc.rule that the
# archive builders (corecrypto, pthread, mockfs) replay; 8796 predates them.
# 0017 backports the proc_get_jit_entitled callback name that Darwin 23's
# libpthread source calls; 8796 still names the field proc_get_pthread_jit_allowlist.
# 0019 is the 8796 port of source-machine-layer.patch's machine list: without
# nos_arm_asm/nos_arm_pmap the source kernel gets neither pmap.o nor the source
# start/cswitch/machine-routines objects that Apple's prelinked kernel supplies.
# 0020 supplies the arm64 kpc backend that the public 8796 tree omits: kperf is
# unconditional and needs kpc, but the PMU lives only in the closed KDK library.
# 0021 defines pmap_pending_preemption() out of line for hygiene builds: pmap.h
# declares it extern, yet the only definition ships in Apple's closed per-SoC
# pmap, so without this the final kernel link fails on five pmap.o call sites.
# 0023 teaches 8796's MakeInc.def the CFLAGS_EXTRA make variable: 10063 added
# it, and the baseline script carries -DXNU_SOURCE_CORECRYPTO14 and the
# boot-progress select in it, so without this the seal contract never compiles
# in and the build stops at the POST HMAC step.
# 0024 backports vfs_getvfs_with_vfsops from the 10063 drop: Apple's 8796
# kernelcache exports it and the prelinked kexts bind it, but the public 8796
# tree never shipped it, so the prelinker is left without a native candidate.
